/* NODE: AVIS.ARTIFACT
   FILE: <WRAPPER_NAME>.art
   NAME: <WRAPPER_NAME>
   ROLE: Wrapper artifact for AVIS .defs definition files

   WRAPS:
       <DEFS_FILE_1>
       <DEFS_FILE_2>
       <DEFS_FILE_3>
       <Add as many as needed>

   IMPORTS:
       <Imported_DEFS_1>
       <Imported_DEFS_2>
       <Imported_DEFS_3>

   DEPENDS:
       <header_or_module_1>
       <header_or_module_2>
       <header_or_module_3>

   SUBSYSTEM:
       FAMILY: AVIS
       LAYER: Definition
       TIER: 0
       STATUS: Active

   IDENTITY:
       VERSION: 1.0
       AUTHOR: AVIS System
       CREATED: <Date>
       UPDATED: <Date>
       SIGNATURE: <Unique ceremonial identifier>

   DESCRIPTION:
       This artifact acts as a wrapper for one or more AVIS .defs files.
       It does not define subsystem identity.
       It provides a unified reference point for template definition sets.
       It is used by AVIS registry and template engines to resolve structure.

   NOTES:
       - Wrapper artifacts do not define EXPORTS.
       - Wrapper artifacts do not define subsystem behavior.
       - Wrapper artifacts exist only to group and expose .defs files.
       - This file is part of the AVIS template infrastructure.

   REGISTRY:
       - Registered as a DEFS wrapper
       - References: <DEFS_FILE_1>, <DEFS_FILE_2>, <DEFS_FILE_3>
       - Provides linkage for: Template resolution systems

   LAW:
       PREFIX: AVIS_
       NAMING: Wrapper artifacts must end in *_WRAP or *_DEF_LINK
       STRUCTURE: Must contain WRAPS block listing .defs files

   HISTORY:
       [v1.0] Initial wrapper template creation

   FUTURE:
       - Additional DEFS categories may be added
       - Wrapper may expand to include template metadata
*/
